{
  "review_note": "riscv-mi restricts the L3 RISC-V model to the integer subset used by riscv-zkvm: no floating point (FPCSR/UserCSR, FP registers, FP instructions, Rounding), no page tables/TLB/virtual translation, no atomics/reservations, no CSR instructions or privileged returns, no timers/counters/interrupts, no FENCE_I and no RV64 word operations other than ADDIW (ADDW, SUBW, SLLW, SRLW, SRAW, SLLIW, SRLIW, SRAIW, MULW, DIVW, DIVUW, REMW, REMUW). The full HOL model remains the main branch's reference. Removed and reduced carriers are not exact HOL ports and carry no @[hol] tag; retained definitions whose equations differ are recorded as handwritten exceptions in rendering-coverage.json.",
